+/// Whether the defender's pending move READS its own HP after this hit, so an
+/// average damage roll would erase reachable positions before that move runs.
+///
+/// Flail and Reversal read it for base power. Substitute reads it as a gate: gen3
+/// refuses the Substitute unless the user is above a quarter of its maximum, so a
+/// roll range straddling that quarter decides whether the Substitute happens at
+/// all -- the cost is paid or not, and `-start` is emitted or not. Collapsing to
+/// the average roll picks one side of that and drops the other from the branch
+/// support entirely (seed 17000037 step 55: eight of sixteen Psychic crit rolls
+/// leave Gyarados' Substitute failing, and the representative roll is on the
+/// succeeding side while Showdown's roll was not).
+fn pending_hp_reading_move(choice: &Choice) -> bool {
+    matches!(
+        choice.move_id,
+        Choices::FLAIL | Choices::REVERSAL | Choices::SUBSTITUTE
+    )
 }
 
